Both fresh definitions compiled successfully; LLVM warned exactly where the candidate over-declared `evalInt` and `evalBool` as total despite non-exhaustive syntax coverage. Concrete K outputs visibly match Python, but my first parser used an over-escaped whitespace regex and falsely reported ten extraction mismatches; I’m correcting that reviewer harness and will preserve both the erroneous run and the corrected rerun transparently. The proof commands completed through the first six claims with `#Top` so far.
